  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media (IRNA, Fars) reported on September 13 that Oman had postponed the Salalah meeting "at the request of some regional countries," with Tehran's MFA explicitly attributing the delay to Bahrain and unnamed Gulf parties. Press TV characterized the postponement as evidence that "GCC states are divided on engaging Iran diplomatically," with no reference to Iran's own agreed participation or to a US role. → supports <span class="cite">F6</span> without move</p>

      <p>IRGC-affiliated media (Tasnim, Mehr) carried without confirmed attribution a claim that a US or Israeli vessel was responsible for the September 13 projectile strike near Hengam Island; UKMTO listed the attacker as unknown. Kayhan's September 14 editorial described the September 9 IAEA Board referral as "the West's last political weapon before its military failure," framing the UNSC track as an escalatory US act rather than a consequence of Iran's nuclear posture. Neither framing produced a new official Iranian diplomatic position. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>No Iranian state outlet covered the i24 poll showing Likud at 27 seats; Iranian domestic coverage of the Israeli election campaign has been near-zero throughout the conflict. IRNA's weekly diplomatic summary mentioned Pezeshkian's September 1 conditional offer to resume ceasefire negotiations "if the US halts attacks," without any follow-up; the offer remains without a US response. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

